            <li><m>g(h(2))=0</m></li>
            <li><m>h(h(2))=2</m></li>
    </ol>
        </p>
        </answer><!--Statement of the answer (don't worry about location in the rendered version)-->
  </exercise><!--End of that exercise-->

    <exercise>
   <statement>
   <p>Suppose <m>g(x)=x^2</m> and <m>h(x)=|x+1|</m> is given in the table below:</p>
        <p>Evaluate each of the following or, if there is insufficient information given to answer the question, state that.
          <ol>
            <li><m>h(g(1))</m></li>
            <li><m>h(g(2))</m></li>
            <li><m>h(g(-1))</m></li>
            <li><m>g(h(-1))</m></li>
            <li><m>h(h(-1))</m></li>
          </ol>
        </p>
   </statement>
     <answer>
        <p>
    <ol>
            <li><m>h(g(1))=2</m></li>
            <li><m>h(g(2))=5</m></li>
            <li><m>h(g(-1))=2</m></li>
            <li><m>g(h(-1))=0</m></li>
            <li><m>h(h(-1))=1</m></li>
    </ol>
        </p>
        </answer><!--Statement of the answer (don't worry about location in the rendered version)-->
  </exercise><!--End of that exercise-->

  <exercise>
   <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=2x+3</m> and <m>g(x)=x^2+x-1</m>. Find each of the following. You do NOT need to simplify.
      <ol>
        <li><m>f(g(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>g(f(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>f(f(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>g(g(x))</m></li>
      </ol>
    </p></statement>
     <answer>
        <p>
    <ol>
        <li><m>f(g(x))=2(x^2+x-1)+3</m></li>
        <li><m>g(f(x))=(2x+3)^2+(2x+3)-1</m></li>
        <li><m>f(f(x))=2(2x+3)+3</m></li>
        <li><m>g(g(x))=(x^2+x-1)^2+(x^2+x-1)-1</m></li>
    </ol>
        </p>
        </answer><!--Statement of the answer (don't worry about location in the rendered version)-->
  </exercise><!--End of that exercise-->

    <exercise>
   <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=|x+3|</m> and <m>g(x)=3x-1</m>. Find each of the following. You do NOT need to simplify.
      <ol>
        <li><m>f(g(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>g(f(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>f(f(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>g(g(x))</m></li>
      </ol>
    </p></statement>
     <answer>
        <p>
    <ol>
        <li><m>f(g(x))=|(3x-1)+3|</m></li>
        <li><m>g(f(x))=3|x+3|-1</m></li>
        <li><m>f(f(x))=||x+3|+3|</m></li>
        <li><m>g(g(x))=3(3x-1)-1</m></li>
    </ol>
        </p>
        </answer><!--Statement of the answer (don't worry about location in the rendered version)-->
  </exercise><!--End of that exercise-->

    <exercise>
   <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=\frac{1}{2}x+1</m> and <m>g(x)=\frac{x+1}{2}</m>. Find each of the following. You do NOT need to simplify.
      <ol>
        <li><m>f(g(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>g(f(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>f(f(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>g(g(x))</m></li>
      </ol>
    </p></statement>
     <answer>
        <p>
    <ol>
        <li><m>f(g(x))=\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{x+1}{2}\right)+1</m></li>
        <li><m>g(f(x))=\frac{\left(\frac{1}{2}x+1\right)+1}{2}</m></li>
        <li><m>f(f(x))=\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{1}{2}x+1\right)+1</m></li>
        <li><m>g(g(x))=\frac{\left(\frac{x+1}{2}\right)+1}{2}</m></li>
    </ol>
        </p>
        </answer><!--Statement of the answer (don't worry about location in the rendered version)-->
  </exercise><!--End of that exercise-->

      <exercise>
   <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=\sqrt{x}</m> and <m>g(x)=4x+5</m>. Find each of the following. You do NOT need to simplify.
      <ol>
        <li><m>f(g(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>g(f(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>f(f(x))</m></li>
        <li><m>g(g(x))</m></li>
      </ol>
    </p></statement>
     <answer>
        <p>
    <ol>
        <li><m>f(g(x))=\sqrt{4x+5}</m></li>
        <li><m>g(f(x))=4\sqrt{x}+5</m></li>
        <li><m>f(f(x))=\sqrt{\sqrt{x}}</m></li>
        <li><m>g(g(x))=4(4x+5)+5</m></li>
    </ol>
        </p>
        </answer><!--Statement of the answer (don't worry about location in the rendered version)-->
  </exercise><!--End of that exercise-->
</exercises>
